    "answer": {
      "short": "$1$\n\nUse complementary angle formulas, then $\\sin^2(37^\\circ)+\\cos^2(37^\\circ)=1$.",
      "worked": "Since $53^\\circ=90^\\circ-37^\\circ$, $\\cos(53^\\circ)=\\sin(37^\\circ)$ and $\\sin(53^\\circ)=\\cos(37^\\circ)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin(37^\\circ)\\cos(53^\\circ)+\\cos(37^\\circ)\\sin(53^\\circ)&=\\sin(37^\\circ)\\sin(37^\\circ)+\\cos(37^\\circ)\\cos(37^\\circ)\\\\\\sin(37^\\circ)\\cos(53^\\circ)+\\cos(37^\\circ)\\sin(53^\\circ)&=\\sin^2(37^\\circ)+\\cos^2(37^\\circ)\\\\\\sin(37^\\circ)\\cos(53^\\circ)+\\cos(37^\\circ)\\sin(53^\\circ)&=1\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
